    {
      "id": "lead-title",
      "name": "Title Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -380
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Handle Contact Form Lead\n\nHandler for one store event: a contact-form submission (event 'contact_form'). It replies to the lead within seconds and moves the lead through the GoHighLevel pipeline.\n\n**Called by:** the main workflow '[GHL Store Automation] | WF1 - Store Events & Win-Back' (its 'Run ... Handler' node, chosen by 'Route By Event Type'), which passes the normalised event together with the store settings. **Standalone-capable:** no.\n\n**Sections on this canvas:**\n1. Reply To The Lead\n\nGoHighLevel work is done by the GHL Adapter workflow (mock or live, chosen by 'ghl_adapter_id') and email by the Email Sender workflow (both called with Execute Workflow). Any failure is reported to the central error handler with THIS workflow's name and the failed node's name.",
        "width": 2800,
        "height": 340,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "lead-sec",
      "name": "Section 1 Note - Reply To The Lead",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Reply to the lead\n\nTriggered by: the main workflow's 'Run ... Handler' node, event 'contact_form'.\n\nWhat it does, step by step:\n1. Creates or updates the contact in GoHighLevel, tags it 'source:contact-form', places it in stage New Lead.\n2. Sends the auto-reply email (through the Email Sender).\n3. If the reply email was sent: sends an SMS too when a phone number was given, then moves the contact to stage Contacted.\n4. If the email could not be sent, the contact stays in New Lead (soft fail, nothing else is lost).",
        "width": 2800,
        "height": 840,
        "color": 4
      }
    }
  ],
